<td><h2>GoodBulk Ltd. (N-OTC: BULK) announces EXTENSION OF DEADLINE FOR SUBMITTING INSTRUCTIONS for the Members' Written Resolution</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2020-04-29 09:37:01</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Reference is made to the "Members' Written Resolution" in lieu of a formal 2020 annual general meeting of GoodBulk Ltd. (the "Company"), where the beneficial shareholders were instructed to returned signed copies of the "Instruction for Members' Written Resolutions" to DNB Bank ASA no later than 30 April 2020 12:00 CEST. The Company today announces that the deadline for submitting instructions to DNB Bank ASA has been extended by eleven-11-days to Monday 11 May 2020 at 16:00 CEST. Please send the instructions to: <br><br>DNB Bank ASA<br>Registrars Dept.<br>P.O. Box 1600 Sentrum<br>0021 Oslo<br>Norway<br><br>or by e-mail: vote@dnb.no<br><br>If you have any questions regarding the procedure for sending instructions, or if you haven't received the Written Resolution including the instruction, please contact DNB Bank ASA at sten.sundby@dnb.no / +47 23 26 80 30.<br><br>About GoodBulk Ltd.<br>GoodBulk, incorporated in Bermuda, is an owner and operator of dry bulk vessels formed in October 2016 for the purpose of owning high quality second hand dry bulk vessels between 50,000–210,000 DWT. Upon completion of the announced dispositions, GoodBulk will control a fleet of 24 dry bulk vessels, including 23 Capesize vessels and one Panamax vessel. Designed to provide an efficient vehicle for investors to access the dry bulk market, all vessels are externally managed by C Transport Maritime S.A.M. a leading third-party manager of dry bulk vessels. GoodBulk is listed on the Norwegian OTC market under the symbol BULK. More information can be found online at www.goodbulk.com.<br><br>Company contact<br>John Michael Radziwill<br>CEO and Chairman<br>GoodBulk Ltd.<br>Tel +377 97 98 59 87<br>Email jmradziwill@goodbulk.com</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
