<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>GoodBulk Ltd. (N-OTC: BULK) Announces Purchase of Common Stock and Delivery of MV Aquaknight and MV Nautical Dream</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2017-04-26 18:14:43</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Hamilton, Bermuda - (April 26, 2017) - GoodBulk Ltd. ("GoodBulk" "Company") (N-OTC: BULK) a recently formed owner and operator of drybulk vessels announced today that on April 24, 2017 the Company entered into an agreement to acquire 394,541 shares of common stock in the market from unaffiliated parties for net consideration of $4,339,951. The shares will remain outstanding and be held in treasury stock. GoodBulk expects to finance this acquisition with available cash on its balance sheet and its credit facility.<br><br>The Company also announced it has taken delivery of two previously announced vessels. The MV Nautical Dream is a 2013 built capesize vessel of approximately 180,000 dwt built by JMU shipyard in Japan. The vessel is expected to be employed in the spot market through the CTH Capesize RSA. The MV Aquaknight is a 2007 built panamax vessel of approximately 75,000 dwt built by Universal Shipyard in Japan. The vessel is expected to be employed in the spot market.<br><br>Following delivery of the announced acquisitions, the Company will control a fleet of ten vessels consisting of seven capesize, one panamax, one ultramax, and one supramax.<br><br>About GoodBulk Ltd.<br><br>GoodBulk is a new owner and operator of drybulk vessels formed in December 2016. The Company's fleet is managed by C Transport Maritime SAM, a leading third party manager in the drybulk shipping industry. GoodBulk is listed on the Norwegian OTC market under the symbol BULK. Further information can be found online at www.goodbulk.com.<br><br>Company contact:<br>Andrew Garcia<br>President and Director<br>GoodBulk Ltd.<br>+377 97 98 59 87<br>ag@goodbulk.com</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="https://goodbulk.com/">
https://goodbulk.com/</a>
<a href="/public/news/16901.pdf">
GB Press Release_20170426.pdf</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>GoodBulk Ltd. (N-OTC: BULK) Announces Acquisition of Panamax Vessel</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2017-04-20 10:31:37</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Hamilton, Bermuda - (April 20, 2017) - GoodBulk Ltd. ("GoodBulk" "Company") (N-OTC: BULK) a recently formed owner and operator of drybulk vessels announced today that it has entered into an agreement to acquire a 2007 built panamax vessel of approximately 75,000 dwt built by Universal Shipyard in Japan. GoodBulk expects to finance this acquisition with available cash on its balance sheet and its credit facility. The vessel is expected to be delivered by the summer of 2017.<br><br>Following completion of the announced acquisition, the Company will control a fleet of ten vessels consisting of seven capesize, one panamax, one ultramax, and one supramax.<br><br>The Company also announced it has taken delivery of the MV Aquakula, a 2007 built supramax vessel of approximately 55,000 dwt built by Oshima Shipyard in Japan which was acquired on February 23, 2017. The vessel is expected to be employed in the spot market through the CTM Supramax RSA.<br><br>About GoodBulk Ltd.<br><br>GoodBulk is a new owner and operator of drybulk vessels formed in December 2016. The Company's fleet is managed by C. Transport Maritime SAM, a leading third party manager in the drybulk shipping industry. GoodBulk is listed on the Norwegian OTC market under the symbol BULK. <br><br>Company contact:<br>Andrew Garcia<br>President and Director<br>GoodBulk Ltd.<br>+377 97 98 59 87<br>ag@goodbulk.com</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
<a href="/public/news/16886.pdf">
GB Press Release_Vessel Acquisition_20170420.pdf</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>BULK: GoodBulk Ltd is registered on the NOTC-list</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2017-03-30 18:07:10</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>GoodBulk Ltd is registered on the NOTC-list as of 31 March 2017 with ticker code “BULK”. The company has issued 13,540,910 common shares each with a par value US$ 1.00, all of which are registered in the VPS with ISIN BMG4095E1003. Based on the last share issue completed on 29 March 2017, the market capitalization is approximately USD 148,950,000, equivalent to approximately NOK 1,266,000,000. The company has entered into an agreement whereby it will be able to use the reporting system as from 31 March 2017.<br>GoodBulk is a new company established by Brentwood Shipping and Trading in December 2016 in partnership with Lantern Capital Partners LP and other partners to create an attractive vehicle for investors to access the drybulk shipping market. GoodBulk currently owns a fleet of nine dry bulk carriers consisting of seven capesize vessels, one ultramax vessel and one supramax vessel. The company’s fleet is managed by C. Transport Maritime SAM, a leading third party manager in the drybulk shipping industry.<br>Please see attached a company presentation of GoodBulk</p></td>
</tr>
